/*
Detection Rule: Azure Privileged Role Assignment Outside PIM
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1098.003 - Account Manipulation: Additional Cloud Roles
Severity: Critical
Description: Detects assignment of high-privilege Azure AD or Azure RBAC roles
outside of Privileged Identity Management (PIM) workflows, or permanent
assignments that bypass PIM's time-limited activation model. Attackers who
gain access to a Global Administrator account will often make direct role
assignments to backdoor accounts for persistent elevated access. All
permanent direct assignments to the monitored high-privilege roles should
be treated as high-confidence malicious activity in environments with PIM.
*/

index=azure_activity sourcetype="azure:audit"
    (operationName="Add member to role"
     OR operationName="Add eligible member to role"
     OR operationName="Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments/write"
     OR operationName="Activate eligible assignment")
    resultType="Success"

| eval actor=coalesce(
    properties.initiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName,
    properties.initiatedBy.app.displayName,
    "unknown_actor")

| eval target_user=coalesce(
    spath(properties.targetResources{0}, "userPrincipalName"),
    spath(properties.targetResources{0}, "displayName"))

| eval role_assigned=spath(properties.targetResources{1}, "displayName")

| eval assignment_type=case(
    operationName="Add eligible member to role",              "PIM Eligible Assignment",
    operationName="Activate eligible assignment",             "PIM Activation",
    operationName="Add member to role",                       "Permanent Direct Assignment",
    operationName="Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments/write", "Azure RBAC Assignment",
    1==1,                                                     "Unknown")

| eval scope=properties.targetResources{0}.id

/* Flag high-privilege roles */
| eval is_privileged=if(match(role_assigned,
    "Global Administrator|Privileged Role Administrator|" .
    "Application Administrator|Exchange Administrator|" .
    "User Access Administrator|Security Administrator|" .
    "Hybrid Identity Administrator|Cloud Application Administrator|" .
    "Owner|Contributor|SharePoint Administrator"),
    1, 0)

| where is_privileged=1

| eval is_pim_bypass=if(assignment_type="Permanent Direct Assignment", 1, 0)

/* Score based on role sensitivity and whether PIM was bypassed */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(is_pim_bypass=1 AND
    match(role_assigned,"Global Administrator|Privileged Role Administrator"), risk_score+70, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(is_pim_bypass=1 AND
    match(role_assigned,"Owner|User Access Administrator"),                    risk_score+60, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(is_pim_bypass=1,                                         risk_score+45, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(role_assigned,
    "Global Administrator|Privileged Role Administrator"),                     risk_score+30, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(role_assigned, "Owner"),                           risk_score+20, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(assignment_type="Azure RBAC Assignment",                 risk_score+10, risk_score)

| stats
    count                       AS assignment_count,
    values(role_assigned)       AS roles_assigned,
    values(assignment_type)     AS assignment_types,
    values(target_user)         AS target_users,
    values(sourceIPAddress)     AS actor_ips,
    values(scope)               AS scopes,
    min(_time)                  AS first_seen,
    max(_time)                  AS last_seen
    by actor, is_pim_bypass, risk_score

| eval alert_title="Privileged Role Assignment Detected: " . actor
| table _time, alert_title, actor, roles_assigned, target_users,
        assignment_types, is_pim_bypass, scopes,
        actor_ips, assignment_count, risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- role_assigned exclusions: Remove lower-risk roles (Contributor) from is_privileged
  check if they produce excessive volume in your environment
- PIM-only environments: Add | where is_pim_bypass=1 to alert only on PIM bypass events
  if your org has fully adopted PIM
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(actor, "ProvisioningConnector|HRSyncApp|IdentityGovernance")
  | where NOT match(roles_assigned, "Contributor|Reader")

FALSE POSITIVES:
- Legitimate IT admin onboarding workflows provisioned by the IAM/identity team
- Approved break-glass account provisioning during incident response
- Automated provisioning via HR-connected identity governance workflows
- Service principal-driven role assignments for approved enterprise applications

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Verify whether a change management ticket exists for this role assignment
2. Confirm the actor's identity and whether their account may be compromised
3. Review what the newly privileged account has done since the assignment was made
4. Immediately remove the unauthorized role assignment via Entra ID portal
5. Revoke all active sessions for the target account that received the elevated role
6. Audit all changes made by the actor and target account since the assignment

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- Actor's full audit trail: index=azure_activity sourcetype="azure:audit"
  properties.initiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName=<actor> earliest=-48h
  | table _time, operationName, resultType, properties.targetResources{0}.displayName
- Target account actions post-assignment: index=azure_activity sourcetype="azure:audit"
  properties.initiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName=<target_user> earliest=<first_seen>
  | table _time, operationName, properties
- OAuth consents by new admin: index=azure_aad sourcetype="azure:aad:audit"
  operationName="Consent to application"
  properties.initiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName=<target_user> earliest=<first_seen>
  | table _time, properties.targetResources{0}.displayName

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- Azure Entra ID Audit Logs (streamed via Diagnostic Settings to Event Hub → Splunk)
- Azure Activity Logs for RBAC assignment events

HIGH-RISK INDICATORS:
- Assignment occurs outside business hours or from an unusual IP for the actor
- Permanent assignment (is_pim_bypass=1) rather than PIM eligible assignment
- Actor's account was involved in a risky sign-in event within the last 24 hours
- Target account was recently created (new account receiving immediate admin role)

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Enforce PIM for all privileged role assignments — zero permanent direct assignments
- Require approval workflow and written justification for Global Admin activations
- Enable Entra ID Access Reviews on a quarterly cadence for all privileged roles
- Alert on any role assignments made by accounts not in the approved IAM team group

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts
- T1136.003 - Create Account: Cloud Account
- T1548.005 - Temporary Elevated Cloud Access

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
